OL,3,GStrathclyde
OL,4,
OL,5,CToday:FA largely dry morning with
OL,6,Fbright intervals. Dry across Argyll in
OL,7,Fthe afternoon with lengthening sunny
OL,8,Fspells but cloudier elsewhere with a
OL,9,Ffew showers developing.
OL,10,
OL,11,CTonight:FShowers in the south soon
OL,12,Fdying out, otherwise a dry evening
OL,13,Fwith sunny spells. Skies becoming
OL,14,Fmostly clear overnight and turning
OL,15,Fchilly, especially in the glens.
OL,16,
OL,17,CSaturday:FA chilly start then a mainly
OL,18,Fdry and bright day with the best of
OL,19,Fthe sunny spells in the south.
OL,20,FCloudier across Argyll with a few
OL,21,Flight showers.
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
